1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elin Jakobsdotter (Bååt)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Elin Jakobsdotter Bååt is supposedly the daughter of Jakob Jacobson Snakenborg and Holmfrid Pedersdotter Pik.?  After further research, I’ve come across a source that shows Holmfried Pedersdotter Pik may not be the mother of Eli
2 CONC n Jakobsdotter Baat.  [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=4579386&photo_id=6000000085090079897&position=1 '''From the Eskilsäter Church, Värmland Funeral Banner Family Board for Lennart Silfversvärd, shows 
2 CONC Holmfrid Pedersdotter Pik’s birth and death dates as 1660-1611?  Either these dates are incorrect or Holmfried Pedersdotter Pik isn’t Elin Jakobsdotter Baat’s mother.  Lennart Silfversvärd Family Banner shows Elin Jakobsdotter (Bå
2 CONC åt)  was born in 1578 and died in 1643, something is definitely wrong here.''']
2 CONT * Jakob Jonsson Til Làng 1540-1604 was Elin’s Stepfather.  Elin’s mother Married Jakob Jonsson, i Lång, Grums, in 1580, when Elin was around 2 years old. In a letter from Duke Carl, dated March 21, 1580, "our beloved Jakob Jonsson
2 CONC " is allowed to use the estates that he and his wife acquired from her father Pär Larsson "which are lying in Värmland", but with the condition that not on any way to dispose of them without first "offering and granting ourselves 
2 CONC to all others". This freedom from taxation has somehow been suspended temporarily and in a letter from Jakob Jonsson to Duke Carl, dated Gripsholm on April 23, 1595, he writes: "I, Jakob Jonsson to Lång, confess that after my K. W
2 CONC ife Hamfrid Pedersdotter, they have squandered her estate were inherited, under Cronan, for the reason that she took me as a married man as an unsalvated man, and Sweden's law contains that a freed woman farmer, then gives tax and
2 CONC  debt as a farmer..." after further attestations, "... with the good consent of my wife and relatives is given and given... His Princely Grace... my wife's inheritance Söderby named in Sone parish on Kållen in Västergötland lies..
2 CONC . to eternal property. . and for further confirmation I request the seals of the honest and virtuous men Nils Månsson and Olaf Cristoffersson as well as my own below this letter..." By this counterstroke it seems that he cleared u
2 CONC p the situation. Frälsegården Mellbyn in Bro (S) was owned in turn by Peder Larsson till Bro, Jakob Jonsson and Elin Jakobsdotter. Kjell Magnell - SoH 1965 no. 2-3 p.415-416. Frälsegården Mellbyn in Bro (S) was owned in turn by Pe
2 CONC der Larsson till Bro, Jakob Jonsson and Elin Jakobsdotter. Died around 1605 in Lång, Grums (S) [1] . Source: Kjell Magnell Family and Family 1965 p.397-420.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000085090079897&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth:	1578, in Lång, Grums, Värmland, Sverige
2 CONT * Elin BÄÄT, was living in 1634.
2 CONT * Death:	1643  in Sweden
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=4579386&photo_id=6000000190279096828&position=0 '''HERE’S THE PROOF THAT ELIN JACOBSDOTTER WAS A Bååt''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000190667403825&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Debate if Elin Jakobsdotter was from the Bååt Family=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Through extensive research from direct line descendants, we have found 3 sources to prove Elin Jakobsdotter was a Baat.  Recently Kjell Magnell in his essay "Pelle i Ramstad, Stårckarna och Elin Jakobsdotter" (Släkt och Hävd 19
2 CONC 65, pp 397-420).  He demonstrated that Elin Jakobsdotter was not from the Baat Family.  
2 CONT
2 CONT This essay has created a debate on the parents of Elin Jakobsdotter Baat:  Here’s three main sources that proves she is the daughter of Jakob Jacobson Snakenborg and Holmfrid Pedersdotter Pik. In the Elgienstierna "The indoctrinat
2 CONC ed Swedish nobility's pedigrees". Volume VIII p.70 it says that Lennart Svenske was married to Elin Jakobsdotter Bååt, daughter of  Demonstrated by Kjell Magnell in the essay "Pelle i Ramstad, Stårckarna och Elin Jakobsdotter" (Sl
2 CONC äkt och Hävd 1965, pp 397-420). According to Magnell, Lennart Svenske was married to Elin Jakobsdotter, who was the daughter of Jacob Jonsson of Lång, Grums (S) and his wife Holmfrid Pedersdotter. In the essay it appears that Holm
2 CONC frid's husband was the deceased rider Jakob Jonsson i Lång, who was of unknown origin.  '''THIS IS TOTALLY INCORRECT!'''  Jakob Jonsson i Lång was her stepfather.  
2 CONT
2 CONT *   '''1st Main Source:'''  shows Elin Jacobsson Baat used her son-in-law Major Carl Jönsson Svinhufvud of Västergötland, Nr.199 Seal to exchange of goods with Carl Bonde on 1633-07-02 in Karlstad (no. 32).  Year and number: 1633 
2 CONC Register: Letter writer register - The National Archives' individual archives and collections from The National Archives' official archive (collective records) in Sweden.
2 CONT *  '''2nd Main Source:'''  is consistent with '''Source: Svenska adelns Ättar-taflor utgifna af Gabriel Anrep, Volume 1, By Gabriel Anrep, Tab 20, page 368.''' shows Elin Jakobsdotter Baat is the daughter of Jakob Jacobson Snakenb
2 CONC org and Holmfrid Pedersdotter Pik.  Elin married Ryttmastaren Lennart Pedersson Svenske, till Satra. 
2 CONT * '''3rd Main Source.''' Holmfrid Pedersdotter Pik sister Margareta Persdotter, who died childless in Bro around 1629 and [https://start.varmlandsrotter.se/varmlandsanor/artiklar/1999_1/ '''shows Elin Jacobsdotter Snakeborg Bååt, 
2 CONC wife of master rider Lennart Persson Svenske, was registered as the nearest heir.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =(1) Main Source=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Elin+Jakobsdotter%2C&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Elin+Jakobsdotter%2C&DatumFran=1578&DatumTill=1643&AvanceradSok=True&page=1&postid=Brev_148266&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 
2 CONC The Swedens Archives of Letter Collections and Correspondence, by Sweden’s  National Archives Database and Digital Research''']
2 CONT
