1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Emma Gertrude  Parritt
2 CONT * Birth:	Aug 1845 - Wooster, Wayne, Ohio, United States
2 CONT * Death:	Apr 24 1936 - Chicago, Cook, Illinois, United States
2 CONT * Parents:	Emelin Morgan Parritt and Emily Hogue
2 CONT * Husband:	Oscar Oldberg
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # Arne Oldberg	
2 CONT # Olga Oldberg
2 CONT # Virgil Oldberg	
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT Chicago Tribune (Chicago, IL) 26 Apr 1936, Sun - BURY MRS. EMMA OLDBERG TODAY; WIDOW OF DEAN
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Mrs. Emma Oldberg, 90 years old, who died Friday in her home at 7808 South Union Ave, will be held today in the chapel at 6237 Normal Blvd. Mrs. Oldberg was the widow of Dr. Oscar Oldberg, founder and dean for
2 CONC  25 years of the school pf pharmacy at Northwestern University. Dr. Oldberg died in 1914.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Oldberg is survived by two sons, Arne Oldberg, composer and conductor, who is head of the department of piano and composition at Northwestern University, and Virgil Oldberg of Detroit, and a daughter, Mrs. Olga Smallwood. In 
2 CONC addition she is survived by 9 grandchildren and 2 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Eric Oldberg, son of Arne Oldberg, is head of the department of neurology and neurological surgery at the University of Illinois school of medicine. Mrs. Oldberg had been a resident in the Auburn Park district since 1886.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
